+# EastSea toolbox presentation assets
+
+These are regeneration inputs for all 17 app pages and the catalog. The
+generator embeds CSS, fonts, dawn mark, favicon and complete font licences
+inside every generated HTML page. Copy a generated app's `index.html` alone
+to deploy it with the same presentation; no sibling assets or build are
+required at deployment. The frontend JavaScript stays inline and
+dependency-free. Documentation links still point to the original toolbox
+repository paths, as they did before the redesign.
+
+`design-tokens.css` and `design-components.css` are generated by the canonical
+EastSea design repository:
+
+```sh
+python3 scripts/gen-design-tokens.py
+python3 scripts/gen-design-tokens.py --check
+```
+
+Copy `design/generated/toolbox/{design-tokens.css,design-components.css}` here
+after changing `design/brand/tokens.json` or `design/brand/components.css`.
+Edit toolbox-specific layout only in `toolbox.css`; do not fork semantic
+colours, typography, spacing, radii, or motion values.
+
+Run `python3 scripts/gen-apps.py` in the toolbox repository after editing its
+page templates. Shared sources are compiled into the generated HTML, so
+presentation changes need regeneration before deployment. Inlining adds
+approximately 140 KB of presentation data per page in exchange for preserving
+the toolbox's original standalone, offline portability.
+
+Appearance follows `prefers-color-scheme`. Set `data-theme="light"` or
+`data-theme="dark"` on the root element when embedding a page in a host with
+an explicit appearance control. Both use the same semantic tokens. Hover
+transitions honor Reduce Motion; the navy plate honors Reduce Transparency.
+There are no continuously running decorative effects.
+
+## Embedded font licences
+
+| Font | File | Licence |
+|---|---|---|
+| Newsreader, Production Type | `fonts/newsreader-latin.woff2` | SIL OFL 1.1, `fonts/OFL-Newsreader.txt` |
+| Geist, Vercel | `fonts/geist-latin.woff2` | SIL OFL 1.1, `fonts/OFL-Geist.txt` |
+| Geist Mono, Vercel | `fonts/geist-mono-latin.woff2` | SIL OFL 1.1, `fonts/OFL-Geist.txt` |
+
+These Latin subsets come from the licensed EastSea site assets. Korean UI
+copy uses the platform Korean fonts in the shared family fallbacks. The
+fonts and SVG are embedded as data URIs in the generated pages. Complete OFL
+text is embedded in each page as well as supplied here; no remote font, image,
+favicon or stylesheet requests are required.
